SUMMARY:Marcus D. Wiley LIVE at Punch Line Philly
DTSTAMP:20260805T111659Z
DTSTART:20260807T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout the Performer\nMarcus D.
	 Wiley is one of the most beloved voices in Christian comedy\, known for h
	is clean\, hilarious\, and deeply relatable stand-up that resonates with a
	udiences of all backgrounds. A radio personality\, comedian\, and motivati
	onal speaker\, Wiley has built a massive following through his work on the
	 nationally syndicated The Rickey Smiley Morning Show\, where he serves as
	 a co-host. \nHis comedy draws from real-life experiences\, faith\, family
	\, and the everyday absurdities of modern life. Wiley has a rare gift for 
	making audiences laugh while also leaving them feeling uplifted and inspir
	ed. His performances are known for being family-friendly yet genuinely fun
	ny — a combination that has earned him fans across generations. \nMarcus D
	. Wiley has performed at comedy festivals\, churches\, and major venues ac
	ross the country. His live shows are high-energy\, interactive\, and packe
	d with the kind of authentic humor that only comes from someone who truly 
	loves making people laugh. \nEvent Details\nDate: Friday\, August 7\, 2026
	 \nTime: 7:00 PM EDT \nVenue: Punch Line Philly — 33 E. Laurel Street\, Ph
	iladelphia\, PA 19123 \nAge Restriction: 21+ with 2-beverage minimum \nTic
	ket Prices: Starting from $30 (plus fees) \nAbout the Venue\nPunch Line Ph
	illy is Philadelphia’s most celebrated comedy club\, located at 33 E. Laur
	el Street in the Northern Liberties neighborhood. The intimate\, 300-seat 
	venue is purpose-built for stand-up comedy\, with a layout that ensures ev
	ery guest has a great view of the stage. \nThe club offers a full bar\, ta
	ble seating\, and a lively atmosphere that sets the perfect tone for a nig
	ht of laughs. The staff is friendly and attentive\, and the venue’s acoust
	ics are designed to make every punchline land perfectly. It’s the kind of 
	place where you feel like you’re part of the show\, not just watching it. 
	\nPunch Line Philly is easily accessible by public transit and has parking
	 available in nearby lots. Doors open 30–45 minutes before showtime — arri
	ve early to get settled and enjoy the pre-show atmosphere. \nWhat to Expec
	t\nMarcus D. Wiley delivers a high-energy\, crowd-interactive performance 
	that blends clean comedy with genuine heart. Expect a show full of relatab
	le stories\, sharp observations\, and the kind of infectious laughter that
	 fills the room from the first minute to the last. \nThe evening will incl
	ude an opening act followed by Marcus D. Wiley’s full headlining set. His 
	shows are known for being inclusive and welcoming — perfect for a diverse 
	audience looking for a great night out without edgy or offensive content. 
	\nThis is a 21+ event with a two-beverage minimum. Tickets are available n
	ow — don’t miss your chance to see one of comedy’s most genuine and entert
	aining performers live in Philadelphia. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range:
	 $30 – $65 (plus fees) \nTickets are available through Ticketmaster (offic
	ial) and VividSeats (resale). Secure your seats today! \nOfficial TicketsR
	esale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commissi
	on at no extra cost to you.\n\nhttps://comedycalendar.com/event/marcus-d-w
	iley-live-at-punch-line-philly/\n\nFrom Comedy Calendar
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/marcus-d-wiley-live-at-punch-line-phil
	ly/
LOCATION:Punch Line Philly\, 33 E. Laurel Street\, Philadelphia\, PA\, 1912
	3\, United States
