SUMMARY:Daniel Sloss: BITTER LIVE at The Wilbur
DTSTAMP:20260805T111659Z
DTSTART:20260807T193000Z
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate l
	inks. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nAbout the Perfor
	mer\nDaniel Sloss is one of the most exciting and critically acclaimed sta
	nd-up comedians working today. The Scottish comedian first burst onto the 
	international scene with his Netflix specials Dark and Jigsaw — both of wh
	ich became global sensations and are widely regarded as two of the best st
	and-up specials of the past decade. \nHis new show BITTER continues his tr
	adition of darkly brilliant\, deeply personal\, and laugh-out-loud funny c
	omedy. Daniel has a rare gift for taking the most uncomfortable subjects —
	 love\, loss\, relationships\, and the human condition — and turning them 
	into comedy that is both hilarious and genuinely moving. \nWith two sold-o
	ut nights at The Wilbur (Aug 7 and Aug 8)\, Daniel Sloss: BITTER is one of
	 the hottest comedy tickets in Boston this summer. Don’t miss your chance 
	to see one of the world’s best stand-up comedians live. \nEvent Details\n\
	nDate: Friday\, August 7\, 2026 (Saturday August 8 show also available)\nT
	ime: 7:30 PM ET\nVenue: The Wilbur\, 246 Tremont St\, Boston\, MA 02116\nT
	ickets from: $81\n\nAbout the Venue\nThe Wilbur is one of Boston’s most be
	loved and intimate comedy venues\, located in the heart of the Theater Dis
	trict at 246 Tremont Street. With a capacity of approximately 1\,000 guest
	s\, The Wilbur offers an up-close and personal experience that is perfect 
	for Daniel’s deeply personal and emotionally resonant performance style. \
	nThe venue features excellent sightlines from every seat\, a full bar\, an
	d a warm\, historic atmosphere that makes every show feel special. Origina
	lly built in 1914\, The Wilbur has been lovingly restored and is now one o
	f the premier comedy destinations on the East Coast. \nParking is availabl
	e at nearby garages in the Theater District\, and the venue is easily acce
	ssible via the MBTA Green and Orange Lines at Boylston and Back Bay statio
	ns. \nWhat to Expect\nExpect a darkly brilliant\, deeply funny\, and emoti
	onally resonant evening of stand-up comedy as Daniel Sloss brings BITTER t
	o The Wilbur. This is a solo performance showcasing Daniel’s signature ble
	nd of dark humor\, personal storytelling\, and the kind of fearless comedy
	 that has made him one of the most talked-about comedians in the world. \n
	Recommended for audiences 18 and older due to mature and dark content. Com
	e ready for a show that will make you laugh\, think\, and feel all at once
	. \nTicket Information\nTickets from $81. Purchase official tickets throug
	h Ticketmaster or find resale tickets via VividSeats. \nOfficial TicketsRe
	sale Tickets\n\nhttps://comedycalendar.com/event/daniel-sloss-bitter-live-
	at-the-wilbur/\n\nFrom Comedy Calendar
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/daniel-sloss-bitter-live-at-the-wilbur
	/
LOCATION:The Wilbur\, 246 Tremont St.\, Boston\, MA\, 2116
